  {"type":"culture","title":"Η επιστήμη στη δημόσια συζήτηση στην Ελλάδα","text":"**Climate** in Greece is no abstraction: the deadly fire at **Μάτι** (2018), the huge **Έβρος** and **Ρόδος** fires (2023), storm **Daniel**'s floods in Thessaly (2023) and summer heatwaves near 45°C have made *κλιματική κρίση* an everyday phrase, alongside *πυρκαγιές, καύσωνας, λειψυδρία* 'water shortage'. Expect any conversation about summer to turn to *η κλιματική αλλαγή* or *οι εμπρησμοί* 'arson'.\n\n**Evolution** is taught in Lyceum biology and, unlike in the US, is not a big culture-war issue; the Orthodox Church has generally not made it a battlefield.\n\n**AI**: Greeks say *τεχνητή νοημοσύνη* (written **ΤΝ** or just *AI*, pronounced 'έι-άι'), but tech talk freely mixes English: *agent, prompt, reels, dms, scroll(άρω)*. English verbs get Greek endings: *τσεκάρω, σκρολάρω, ποστάρω, γκουγκλάρω*. In writing, the style guides prefer *ψηφιακός πράκτορας* for 'agent', but almost nobody says it."}
